From: MYOS C8 maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mediatek: initialize max_mtu before DSA probing

DSA requests a 1504-byte master MTU during switch registration. Initializing
max_mtu only in mtk_open leaves the default 1500 limit during that request,
which fails with EINVAL. Publish the receive-buffer limit before registration;
retain the existing interface-specific refinement in mtk_open.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
@@ -6323,6 +6323,12 @@
 	mac->phylink = phylink;
 
+	/* Allow DSA tag overhead before register_netdev() probes the switch.
+	 * mtk_open() can refine this limit after the interface is configured.
+	 */
+	eth->netdev[id]->max_mtu = min_t(unsigned int, MTK_MAX_RX_LENGTH,
+				      MTK_MAX_RX_LENGTH_2K) - MTK_RX_ETH_HLEN;
+
 	SET_NETDEV_DEV(eth->netdev[id], eth->dev);
 	eth->netdev[id]->watchdog_timeo = 5 * HZ;
 	eth->netdev[id]->netdev_ops = &mtk_netdev_ops;
 	eth->netdev[id]->base_addr = (unsigned long)eth->base;
